    {
      "id": "mtn-guide",
      "type": "adventure",
      "x": 1200,
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "lines": [
        "Higher than it looks, colder than it feels. You are the searcher, then.",
        "They went over — or under, none could say. The peak breaks two ways ahead.",
        "The high climb is shortest, if your hands are trained for it. The caves are kinder to those who are not."
      ],
      "choices": [
        "Which way would you go?",
        "Press on"
      ],
      "responses": [
        "Me? I would go where my hands are strongest. So should you.",
        "Then go warm and go quick. Storms come fast up here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mtn-wolves",
      "type": "creature",
      "kind": "wolf",
      "count": 2,
      "x": 1800
    },
    {
      "id": "mtn-oathstone",
      "type": "adventure",
      "x": 2200,
      "speaker": "Oathstone",
      "lines": [
        "A standing stone, waist-high, worn smooth on its eastern face by generations of hands.",
        "Names are scratched into it, hundreds, layered over each other. The custom is old: leave your name, swear to come back for it."
      ],
      "choices": [
        "Carve your name and swear",
        "Leave the stone unmarked"
      ],
      "responses": [
        "The knife is blunt and the granite is hard and it takes a long time. That seems to be the point.",
        "You put your palm flat against the cold face of it and move on."
      ],
      "outcomes": [
        {
          "mark": {
            "oath": "sworn"
          }
        },
        {
          "mark": {
            "oath": "none"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mtn-bram",
      "type": "adventure",
      "x": 3100,
      "speaker": "Shepherd",
      "lines": [
        "Hoy — off the track, there's a slide above you.",
        "I've kept sheep on this pass eleven years. This spring something came down out of the high country and took nine of them in a night. Not wolves. Wolves don't take nine.",
        "There's nothing left up here worth minding. I've a good spear and I'd rather use it walking than standing."
      ],
      "choices": [
        "Come with us",
        "Keep your pass, we'll keep the road"
      ],
      "responses": [
        "Bram, he says, and shoulders the spear like a man glad to be rid of a hill.",
        "He nods, and does not look surprised, and goes back to counting what he has left."
      ],
      "outcomes": [
        {
          "companion": "bram",
          "mark": {
            "bram": "joined"
          }
        },
        {}
      ]
    },
